From e563ca492c41fbadf6380e146a21b1cd4664016e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:52:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 28/29] freebsd: show host devices asked for by hostPath or CRI
 devices through devfs

A hostPath volume on the host's devfs was a nullfs mount: a view of every
host device past the container's devfs ruleset, whose open and ioctl
reached the drivers (the kernel now refuses opens through nullfs). Do what
Linux's device cgroup does with devfs instead:

- a device or device directory at its own path below /dev: unhide it in
  the container's devfs;
- hostPath /dev elsewhere (/host/dev): a second devfs with the ruleset
  and rules of the container's /dev (all devices if privileged);
- anything else (another name, another directory): an error.

CRI devices (device plugins) are unhidden the same way. The privileged
ruleset=0 now targets the /dev devfs, not the first devfs mount.
